  "answer": "This has been reported before. It is not a DWM/MPO regression, and the Independent Flip discussion (#19010) is a separate topic. Terminal#19250 describes the same thing: content behind the window flashes when a pane is created with Shift+Alt+D. It was closed as a duplicate of terminal#12334, 'The open pane animation background is transparent'. The cause is the pane open animation, where the background is briefly transparent while the new pane animates in. The maintainers said a real fix would need a different UI framework, so don't expect one soon. Follow #12334 for updates. The archive doesn't show a confirmed workaround. The setting 'Disable pane animations' (the `disableAnimations` option) controls pane animations. I'd try it, but I haven't confirmed that it removes the flash. Your PresentMon data is unlikely to change this diagnosis."
 },
